## Android adaptation

The Android adaptation layer (`src/SMAPI/Mobile/`) follows the design approach
of the following LGPL-3.0 projects:

- [NRT-SMAPI-Android](https://github.com/NRTnarathip/SMAPI-Android-1.6)
  (by NRTnarathip) — Android adaptation layer organization, frame-based mod
  loading, mod fix framework, audio (NVorbis/OGG) support, etc.
- [ZaneYork/SMAPI](https://github.com/ZaneYork/SMAPI) — early Android
  adaptation reference (e.g. PlatformAssemblyMap Android handling).

Both upstream projects are distributed under LGPL-3.0, consistent with this
project's license. This project re-integrates and adapts the design on top of
upstream SMAPI 4.5.2.

The companion Android launcher (which loads this SMAPI into the game process)
is an independent clean-room implementation inspired by the general approach
of [NRT-SMAPILoader](https://github.com/NRTnarathip/SMAPI-Launcher) (GPL-3.0);
it does not contain code from that project.

